Original commit body from a7c9f0e89270a4edc8b552bdcd96ffe528985263:

`svc = Service(); svc.conn.request(q)` -- or `def run(svc: Service)`, or two hops
through a project-class field, or `self.svc.sock.sendall(x)` -- now names the
module Service.__init__ gave the field (`http.client.HTTPConnection`,
`socket.socket`) in the module slot, the same map that already typed
`self.conn` INSIDE Service. `_receiver_type` answers a dotted field path
(`_dotted_receiver_name`) from `external_var_types`; the walker writes
`<local>.<field>` keys at the binding site (`_bind_project_class_fields`:
purged on rebind, pruned with a shadowed root, one hop through a project-class
field).

The red tests exposed why this never worked across files: the per-class field
maps were built inside `_extract_edges`, per file, so a class imported from
another file had no map, and building at edge time is order-dependent. They
are now built once per repo before any file's edges
(`_collect_class_field_maps`, re-keyed by class-symbol id so a same-short-name
class in two files is unambiguous), and the three per-file param-type
resolvers that builder needs moved verbatim into `_make_param_type_helpers`.

A derivation rooted at `self.<field>` (`out_file = self.out_dir / name`) is
typed for the first time as a side effect: the key existed but only the
self-branch emitter read it.

